desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Apex Specify Sharing Level"
	title_zh: "检测到 Apex 类未显式声明共享级别",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-apex-specify-sharing-level"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `specify-sharing-level` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/apex/lang/security/ncino/sharing/SpecifySharingLevel.yaml).
Original message: Every Apex class should have an explicit sharing mode declared. Use the `with sharing` or `without sharing` keywords on a class to specify whether sharing rules must be enforced. Use the `inherited sharing` keyword on an Apex class to run the class in the sharing mode of the class that called it.

CWE: CWE-284: Improper Access Control
References:
- https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.apexcode.meta.apexcode/apex_classes_keywords_sharing.htm
- https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/284.html
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Declare `with sharing`, `without sharing`, or `inherited sharing` explicitly on every Apex class.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.cls": <<<POS
public class ExampleController {
}
POS
	"safefile://neg.cls": <<<NEG
public with sharing class ExampleController {
}
NEG
)

${*.cls}.pattern_regex_not(/(?:private|public|global)[\s\S]*?\sclass\s[\s\S]*?\{/, /(?:private|public|global)[\s\S]*?\b(?:with|without|inherited)\s+sharing\b[\s\S]*?\sclass\s[\s\S]*?\{/, /(?:private|public|global)[\s\S]*?\sclass\s[\s\S]*?\bextends\s+Exception\b[\s\S]*?\{/) as $p0
${*.apex}.pattern_regex_not(/(?:private|public|global)[\s\S]*?\sclass\s[\s\S]*?\{/, /(?:private|public|global)[\s\S]*?\b(?:with|without|inherited)\s+sharing\b[\s\S]*?\sclass\s[\s\S]*?\{/, /(?:private|public|global)[\s\S]*?\sclass\s[\s\S]*?\bextends\s+Exception\b[\s\S]*?\{/) as $p1
$p0 + $p1 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Apex Specify Sharing Level",
	title_zh: "检测到 Apex 类未显式声明共享级别",
	message: "Apex class does not explicitly declare a sharing level.",
}
